#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:188
msgid "excimer (function-level profiling)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:189
msgid "The one to install. Which exact FUNCTION is burning the time - including inside theme template files, which no other instrument can see - with each function attributed to its plugin, split by which plugin was driving it, and broken down per request phase. A sampling profiler with negligible overhead, maintained by the Wikimedia Foundation and run on every Wikipedia page view, so it profiles during normal measurement without distorting the numbers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:193
msgid "In use: every profiled page carries the \"By function\" view, and the untimed parts of each request phase expand to the functions sampled inside them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:194
msgid "Needs a one-off install by you or your host - the steps below are generated for this exact server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:198
msgid "Query plans (EXPLAIN)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:199
msgid "Shows WHY a query is slow: a missing index, a temporary table, a filesort. Also catches queries that are fast today but will not scale."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:202
msgid "Built in. Needs nothing installed and no extra database permission."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:206
msgid "MySQL query fingerprints"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:207
msgid "MySQL's own normalised query statistics: how many rows were REALLY examined per query, not the optimiser's estimate, and which queries used no index."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:215
msgid "tideways_xhprof (exact call counts)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:216
msgid "Counts every function call exactly, which is what proves a plugin is running the same query in a loop. Higher overhead than excimer, so it is for one page at a time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:220
msgid "The original xhprof is present. tideways_xhprof is the better-maintained successor. Not read by the plugin: exact call counts are a planned deep-dive mode, and sampling answers most questions without the overhead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:221
msgid "Not read by the plugin: exact call counts are a planned deep-dive mode, and sampling answers most questions without the overhead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:225
msgid "SPX (standalone profiler)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:226
msgid "A self-hosted profiler with its own flamegraph and timeline interface. Nothing leaves your server. We detect it and link to it rather than rebuilding what it already does well."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:313
msgid "1. Switch performance_schema on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:314
msgid "MariaDB ships with it off. This needs a MySQL restart, so it is the one step that causes a moment of downtime."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:319
msgid "1. Grant read access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:319
msgid "2. Grant read access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:320
msgid "Run as a database administrator. This is READ-ONLY access to performance statistics - it grants nothing over your site's data and cannot change anything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:366
msgid "1. Install the package"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: detected operating system, 2: detected PHP version
#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:369
#, php-format
msgid "Excimer is packaged for this distribution: nothing to compile, no ini file to write (the package enables itself), and it updates with the rest of the system, where a hand-compiled copy silently stops loading when PHP is upgraded. The command targets PHP %2$s because that is what this site runs - on servers carrying several PHP versions, the unversioned package installs for the newest one instead, which leaves this site without the extension. Detected: %1$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:376
msgid "2. Restart PHP"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the detected PHP SAPI
#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:379
#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:471
#, php-format
msgid "A reload is not enough for a new extension. Detected SAPI: %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:385
msgid "3. Check it worked"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:386
msgid "The versioned binary matters: plain `php` on the command line can be a different PHP than the site runs. Then press Re-check on this page - that is the authoritative test, because it asks the exact PHP process serving this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:401
msgid "tideways_xhprof has never been on PECL, so it is built from source. It is free and open source (Apache 2.0) and sends nothing anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:406
msgid "SPX is not on PECL, so it is built from source. Licence: GPL-3."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:430
msgid "1. Install the build tools"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: detected operating system
#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:433
#, php-format
msgid "The extension is compiled on this server, so it needs the PHP development headers. Detected: %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:441
msgid "2. Build and install"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:447
msgid "2. Install the extension"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:448
msgid "Excimer is free and open source (Apache 2.0) and sends nothing anywhere - a local extension, not a service. PECL itself is deprecated and excimer 1.2.6 is the last version published there, but on this system it is still the shortest working path (the maintained successor is PIE: pie install wikimedia/excimer). If this step fails with \"shtool ... does not exist or is not executable\", your server mounts /tmp with noexec (a common hardening default) - temporarily allow execution there for the build, then restore it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:459
msgid "3. Enable it"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the ini scan directory detected on this server
#: includes/class-sspa-tools.php:462
#, php-format
